+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Connecting to the LDAP server
=============================

The "url" key of the table configuration selects how table-ldap talks to
the LDAP server:

    url: ldap://host[:port]       plain text, default port 389
    url: ldaps://host[:port]      LDAP over TLS, default port 636
    url: ldap+tls://host[:port]   plain connection upgraded with StartTLS,
                                  default port 389

For ldaps:// and ldap+tls:// the server certificate is verified against the
system CA bundle (/etc/ssl/cert.pem) and must be valid for the host name
given in the URL, so use a name from the certificate, not an IP address.
To verify against a different CA bundle (e.g. a private CA), add:

    ca_file: /etc/ssl/my-ldap-ca.pem

If the TLS handshake or the certificate check fails, the connection is not
used; there is no fallback to plain text.  As with an unreachable server,
the failure is logged, the lookup returns an error and the next lookup tries
to connect again.  table-ldap also keeps running when the server is
unreachable at startup.

Example:

    url: ldaps://ldap.example.com
    username: cn=smtpd,ou=services,dc=example,dc=com
    password: secret
    basedn: ou=people,dc=example,dc=com
